  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Agr 1803.01 Apiary Identification. Beekeepers shall print, stencil, or brand their name, mailing address, and phone number directly on the outside of the hive body, the underside of the top covers, or a sign prominently displayed in the apiary to facilitate communication by inspectors and emergency personnel.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Agr 1800) #5802, eff 3-25-94, EXPIRED: 3-25-00\n\nNew. #7284, eff 5-24-00, EXPIRED: 5-24-08\n\nNew. #10586, eff 5-13-14; ss by #13978, eff 5-23-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/agr1800.html"
